{number: 137}
{title: Softly and Tenderly Jesus is Calling}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Softly and tenderly [F] Jesus is [C] calling,
Calling for you and for [G7] me;
[C] See, on the portals He's [F] waiting and [C] watching,
Watching for [G7] you and for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7] Come home, [C] come home,
[D7] Ye who are weary, [G7] come home;
[C] Earnestly, tenderly, [F] Jesus is [C] calling,
Calling, O [G7] sinner, come [C] home!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Why should we tarry when [F] Jesus is [C] pleading,
Pleading for you and for [G7] me?
[C] Why should we linger and [F] heed not His [C] mercies,
Mercies for [G7] you and for [C] me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Time is now fleeting, the [F] moments are [C] passing,
Passing from you and from [G7] me;
[C] Shadows are gathering, [F] deathbeds are [C] coming,
Coming for [G7] you and for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
